LEGENDARY, AS SIX SKINS -- the measured output of
dev/legendary/BUILD_LEGENDARY_PAINT.luau, one run per framing.

Both runs calibrate the same six shapes to the same 45% coverage, so the two
tables differ only in the body size the cells were built at. The feature columns
are reported at BOTH framings from either run, which is the whole point of
having two of them: a feature that resolves at 7 studs and not at 16 is the
failure this rig exists to catch, and it cannot be caught by a number that only
knows about the build it is in.

